the target language is: prolog.

% Regression fixture: colouring user-assumed conditions in explanations.
% "alice is happy" is derivable (the rule proves it from "alice is nice"), so it
% normally shows as a proven (green) node. When a scenario ASSUMES it ("it is
% unknown whether alice is happy"), the explanation must show that node as an
% assumption (unknown / yellow) EVEN THOUGH it is provable — reflecting the Assume
% checkbox's "consider this unknown, and assume it true". This is display-only: the
% answers and the unknowns list are unchanged (the rule still proves it).

the templates are:
    *a person* is happy.
    *a person* is nice.

the knowledge base assumed_coloring includes:
    a person is happy if the person is nice.

scenario derived is:
    alice is nice.
    happy expects answers ["alice is happy"] and unknowns [].

scenario assumed is:
    alice is nice.
    it is unknown whether alice is happy.
    happy expects answers ["alice is happy"] and unknowns [].

query happy is:
    which person is happy.
